==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|per-|gloss1=through|sonō|gloss2=make a noise, sound, resound}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|personō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|personō|personāre|personuī|personātum|conj=1}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I [[sound]] through and through, [[resound]], [[ring]].
#* '''1832''', [[w:Pope Gregory XVI|Gregory XVI]], ''[[:w:Mirari Vos|Mirari Vos]]''
#*: '''Personant''' horrendum in modum academiae ac gymnasia novis opinionum monstris, quibus non occulte amplius et cuniculis petitur catholica fides […]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I make a sound on a [[musical instrument]], [[play]], sound.
# {{lb|la|transitive}} I [[fill]] with sound, make resound.
# {{lb|la|transitive|rare}} I [[cry out]], [[call]] aloud.

